<header><p class="st-kicker">chiefdom · British Isles</p><h1 class="st-title">Nagnatae</h1><p class="st-meta">100 CE – 200 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">People of north-west Ireland recorded by Ptolemy, who also names a notable town of theirs called Nagnata.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/geography-ptolemy">Ptolemy's Geography</a> of about 150 places the Nagnatae on the north-west coast of Ireland, roughly in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/county-sligo">Sligo</a> or north <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/county-mayo">Mayo</a>, and lists a settlement called Nagnata, which he describes as a notable town. His information came from earlier sailors' reports on the Atlantic coast.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Nothing is recorded of their rulers, economy or customs. The identification of Nagnata is disputed; sites around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sligo-bay">Sligo Bay</a> have been suggested, and some versions of the text spell the people Magnatae, which has led to other proposed meanings. The region was rich in older monuments such as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carrowmore">Carrowmore</a> tombs.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>No later source mentions the Nagnatae. Their area later lay within the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-connacht">Kingdom of Connacht</a>, ruled by branches of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/connachta">Connachta</a> dynasties.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/nagnatae.jpg" alt="Nagnatae" width="320" height="383"><figcaption>Image: Nicolaus Germanus · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ptolemy_Cosmographia_1467_-_Ireland.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>100 CE – 200 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/2nd-century">2nd century</a> – <a href="/centuries/3rd-century">3rd century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>chiefdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Celtic polytheism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Goidelic Celtic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/ireland">Ireland</a></dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=150&amp;focus=nagnatae" aria-label="Nagnatae on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4522 334 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Nagnatae lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4842 590h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M4842 590h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Ireland. <a href="/atlas?year=150&amp;focus=nagnatae">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

